And the heal double-read: IMPORTANT (perf on resume hot path) or SUGGESTION? Let me be decisive: it doubles the primary read on every open of any rotated session — a session ≥80MB. Resume already reads ~95MB+parts. The heal's extra full read adds up to +95MB I/O per resume, on the exact sessions the PR targets. The repo logs resume_timing because resume perf is tracked. I'll file IMPORTANT.

