`bin/fah.dart` wires `onRotationWarning → stderr.writeln`, but the flutter app (`AgentService`) never sets the hook — a hard-cap truncation ("dropped N oldest record(s)") is invisible to app users even though it permanently drops session history. The precedent for "never silent" host-visible drops is the image registry's `AppLog` (issue #195 F4). One line in `AgentService` boot (e.g. `JsonlSessionStorage.onRotationWarning = (m) => AppLog.warn(m)`, or routed into the session log sink) closes the gap; the default-null design makes this a safe follow-up, not a merge blocker.
